.TH buffer_free 3
.SH NAME
buffer_free \- release memory allocated by a buffer
.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <buffer.h>

void \fBbuffer_free\fP(buffer *\fIb\fP);
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBbuffer_free\fP releases the internal buffer space allocated to the
buffer structure pointed to by \fIb\fP. It uses \fBalloc_free\fP
to free the memory associated with the buffer's data area (\fIb->x\fP)
and sets the pointer \fIb->x\fP to 0.

If \fIb->x\fP is already 0, \fBbuffer_free\fP does nothing.

.SH SEE ALSO
alloc(3), buffer(3), buffer_init_free(3)